<title>RUSSIA: Russia big farms gross grain harvest at 64.8 mln T.</title>
<headline>Russia big farms gross grain harvest at 64.8 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's large farms, which account for 93 percent of the total area sown to grain, had threshed 64.8 million tonnes bunker weight of grain as of October 7, State Statistics Committee figures showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The committee released the following figures for output on formerly state-run collective farms-</p>
<p>	  PACE OF RUSSIAN GRAIN HARVEST AS OF OCT 7</p>
<p>				   1996	1995	  1994</p>
<p>Cut (excl. maize,</p>
<p>  in million hectares)	40.2     41.7	  45.3</p>
<p>   as pct of sown area	83	 85	    91</p>
<p>Threshed</p>
<p>  (million hectares)	  39.4     41.5	  44.7</p>
<p>(million tonnes,</p>
<p>   bunker weight)	     64.8     60.5	  77.6</p>
<p>  as pct of sown area	 82	 84	    89</p>
<p>  as pct of cut area	  98	 99	    99</p>
<p> Yield (tonnes/hectare)     1.64     1.46	  1.73</p>
<p> Maize (harvested, million</p>
<p>  hectares)			5.3	5.5	   6.4</p>
<p>  as pct of sown area	 80	 86	    86</p>
<p>The committee said that 3.1 million hectares of grain remained to be harvested, mostly in Siberia.</p>
<p>Winter crops had been sown to 11.5 million hectares so far, 8 percent below the level at this time last year.</p>
<p>Nearly 25.9 million hectares had been prepared for spring sowing, below the 31.6 million ready at this time last year.</p>
<p>-- Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
